  "problem": "The same-connection status read could report an untrusted owned folder but the formal application had no shared, explicitly reviewed trust decision operation.",
  "change": {
    "entry": "One common review and separate confirmation, showing only finite actual offered choices and persistent scope, instruction/configuration/hook reload consequences. Cancelling review dispatches no decision.",
    "command": "session_workspace_access_decide",
    "availability": "Optional reviewed decisionManagement capability, separate from statusQuery and the official initialize declaration. Typed unavailable withdraws only this matching owner decision capability.",
    "choices": ["trust_cwd", "trust_repo", "decline"],
    "scope": "Same Agent, native conversation, connection, cwd and selected service; read-time scope comparison and original actor guard recheck precede the one actual dispatch. No atomic repository-root CAS or filesystem isolation is claimed.",
    "lifetime": "AccountScope protects the dispatched operation until a witnessed actual response or original process reap. A transient single-operation response witness preserves the incoming envelope and is not an event ledger. SDK-local failure alone does not release an unconfirmed write.",
    "prewriteRead": "Caller abandonment or expiry before any write drops shared effect protection while the original read remains observed; no later Commit is possible.",
    "configuration": "Trust receipt does not confirm model/permissions or continue the queue. Grant emits existing configuration-needs-recheck protection before send. Actual reload notification completeness remains unverified.",
    "implicitActions": "No new/load/reconnect/auth/model prompt/configuration setter/retry/rollback/queue continuation. Decline is a persistent decision, not review cancellation.",
    "deliveryDeadlineSeconds": 20
  },
